Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: hyprland-preview-share-picker
Upstream-Contact: WhySoBad, https://github.com/WhySoBad/hyprland-preview-share-picker/issues
Source: https://github.com/WhySoBad/hyprland-preview-share-picker
Comment:
 The source package carries three trees: the program (the release tarball),
 hyprland-protocols/ (the git submodule lib/hyprland-protocols, shipped as the
 component "hyprland-protocols") and vendor/ (the crates from Cargo.lock,
 shipped as the component "vendor" so the build needs no network). The Files
 stanzas for vendor/ group the crates by their Cargo.toml license field; each
 crate's copyright holders are the authors named in that crate's Cargo.toml and
 the license files inside the crate's directory.
 .
 The hyprland and hyprland-macros crates are GPL-3.0-or-later and are linked
 statically into the binary, so the binary as a whole is distributed under the
 GPL-3+, although the program's own source is MIT.

